# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .gitignore — what must never enter version control.
# READING ORDER: 3 (skim after PROMPT.md and README.md)
#
# WHY this file matters for a learning codebase:
#   The single most dangerous thing you can commit is a secret (an API key).
#   This app also generates local state (a SQLite DB, model workspaces) that is
#   personal to your machine and would only create noise or conflicts in git.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Secrets: NEVER commit real keys. Only .env.example (with blank values) is tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Backend local state (recreated on demand; see db.py). Not shared between machines.
backend/data/
backend/**/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
backend/**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
backend/.venv/
*.egg-info/

# --- Frontend build + dependency artifacts (reproducible from package.json).
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

# --- Linux release artifacts (rebuilt from the locked source tree).
linux_install/dist/

# --- The user's retyping scratch space (Section 1, rule 8). Personal, not shared.
learning/retyped/*
!learning/retyped/.gitkeep

# --- OS / editor cruft.
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
